From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yodaliu <yodaliu@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 17:18:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 15/15] usb: dwc3-msm: also disable the power event irq
 synchronously on suspend

dwc3_msm_suspend() calls disable_irq() on the power event irq right after
disable_irq_nosync(), so the irq disable depth stays raised by one after
resume.

Reconstructed from the stock FiiO M21 FW 1.1.0 dwc3-msm module.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-msm-core.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-msm-core.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-msm-core.c
index 89dc4d47ffc..80d6b2ba595 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-msm-core.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-msm-core.c
@@ -3933,6 +3933,7 @@ static int dwc3_msm_suspend(struct dwc3_msm *mdwc, bool force_power_collapse)
 
 	/* disable power event irq, hs and ss phy irq is used as wake up src */
 	disable_irq_nosync(mdwc->wakeup_irq[PWR_EVNT_IRQ].irq);
+	disable_irq(mdwc->wakeup_irq[PWR_EVNT_IRQ].irq);
 
 	dwc3_set_phy_speed_flags(mdwc);
 	/* Suspend HS PHY */
